comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T23:17:20.508Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: exact all-status GH-1132 search returned zero items; broader all-status searches found annotation grammar, output-bounding, dedupe-audit, and lock-retry owners but none owns idempotent annotation mutation. GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1132. This item extends the canonical SDK annotation kernel and multi-agent safety lineages rather than duplicating them."
  "2026-08-27T23:25:34.767Z","harness:codex","TDD red: focused comments suite now proves missing idempotent mutation semantics. The first --if-absent call has no changed receipt, the retry appends again instead of preserving history bytes, and non-append invocations incorrectly accept the option. Command: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/commands/comments-command.spec.ts; result 43 passed, 2 expected failures."
  "2026-08-27T23:54:24.815Z","harness:codex","Evidence: implemented SDK-owned lock-scoped comment idempotency with CLI --if-absent, MCP options.ifAbsent, canonical schemas, completions, stable refusal catalog, and documented changed receipts. Fresh CLI+SDK acceptance proved one history event across exact retries; a real PM_MCP_PROFILE=full stdio process returned changed true/1 then false/0. Focused SDK/CLI/MCP/completion tests passed 162/162, concurrency proved one writer and five no-ops, static complexity passed <=16, docstrings passed 567/567 source, 4507/4507 exports, 8187/8187 members, and full coverage passed 585 files / 8072 tests / exact 100/100/100/100 (59928 statements, 45132 branches, 12463 functions, 57710 lines)."
  "2026-08-27T23:56:45.196Z","harness:codex","Release-input evidence: npm registry reports pm-changelog 2026.8.17 as latest; package install verification passed with fresh topology activation and CHANGELOG generation was idempotent (changed true, then check unchanged). pnpm audit reported zero known vulnerabilities; package artifact, agent-task token, command grammar, flag parity/lexicon, and docs-link gates passed."
  "2026-08-28T00:05:27.806Z","harness:codex","Defect-evidence remediation: classified the escaped behavior as production_defect and bound it to the comment-append-idempotency gate. Its negative control removes the writer-lock lookup or skipNoop path; sequential history-byte, six-writer concurrency, CLI, MCP, full coverage, hosted static/coverage, and Windows Node 24 checks must then fail. No waiver is used."
  "2026-08-28T00:46:31.756Z","harness:codex","Final universal-annotation evidence: comments, text/JSON notes, and learnings now share SDK-owned lock-scoped ifAbsent semantics through CLI and MCP transports. CI=1 pnpm quality:static passed the 12/12 replication gate, 3053-entry flag lexicon, zero help-token growth, public SDK/contracts, package boundaries, grammar, refusal, graph, and record-integrity gates. Full coverage passed 585 files / 8076 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (59928 statements, 45125 branches, 12463 functions, 57710 lines). A fresh /tmp CLI workspace proved changed true then false and stable history hashes for all families; direct PmClient proved true-to-false receipts; packed artifact, npx smoke, and pnpm audit (0 vulnerabilities) passed."
  "2026-08-28T01:46:34.667Z","harness:codex","Closeout continuation: the linked static false-fail recorded on this item was isolated to CLI transport-floor RSS admission and is now repaired by closed item pm-pz49xc. Its final 4/4 linked run passed focused 7/7, the live six-operation floor, exact 585-file/8076-test 100/100/100/100 coverage, and CI=1 repository static quality. The earlier failed receipts remain immutable reproduction evidence; annotation implementation behavior was not changed by the gate repair."
  "2026-08-28T02:48:26.861Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review reconciliation: the six historical failed runs are immutable TDD and transport-floor reproduction receipts. Reopened and claimed this item to record one terminal passing run across all four currently linked commands after pm-pz49xc and pm-j8vq corrected the two independent static-gate failures."
  "2026-08-28T03:21:03.920Z","harness:codex","Review correction evidence: documented options.ifAbsent parity in pm_notes and pm_learnings MCP discovery, regenerated the built contract snapshot, and recorded one clean linked run after the earlier failed attempts. All four linked gates pass on the exact source state: contracts plus SDK surface, exact full coverage, tracker-context static quality, and 7 focused files / 230 tests. The failed intermediate run was caused by regenerating the snapshot before rebuilding; rebuild-then-regenerate corrected that generated-state ordering."
  "2026-08-28T04:01:21.589Z","harness:codex","TDD red for schema-version drift: the strict action schema already exposes additive ifAbsent parameters while PM_TOOL_PARAMETERS_SCHEMA_VERSION remains 4.9.0. A focused semantic-version ratchet expects 4.10.0 and failed exactly on 4.9.0 in the combined review test run."
  "2026-08-28T04:15:15.096Z","harness:codex","TDD and review evidence: added an exact schema-version assertion that failed at 4.9.0 after the additive annotation ifAbsent contract. Advanced PM_TOOL_PARAMETERS_SCHEMA_VERSION to 4.10.0, regenerated the full contract fixture, and refreshed the public SDK surface with an explicit breaking-literal compatibility acknowledgment. Focused acceptance passed 29 tests; contracts:check and sdk:surface:check passed; the exact repository run passed 8,081 tests across 585 files at 100/100/100/100 coverage, and CI-mode static quality passed."
  "2026-08-28T05:09:44.555Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence: CodeRabbit found the MCP schemas permit flat ifAbsent beside nested options.add, but runtime normalization only preserved nested ifAbsent. The correction will hoist flat idempotency for comments, notes, and learnings while retaining explicit nested-option precedence."
  "2026-08-28T05:10:40.538Z","harness:codex","TDD red: flat ifAbsent beside nested options.add was absent from the final runComments options; the combined comments/notes/learnings transport regression failed exactly on the first flat annotation assertion."
  "2026-08-28T05:36:49.766Z","harness:codex","Correction evidence: focused MCP residual coverage proves nested and flat ifAbsent normalization for comments, notes, and learnings; the combined focused suite passes 294 tests; full coverage passes 8,083 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; fresh-directory public SDK acceptance proved one persisted annotation and a no-effect duplicate for every family."
  "2026-08-28T06:38:34.567Z","harness:codex","Exact-head release-note reconciliation: the canonical title now says ifAbsent/--if-absent deduplication is opt-in and that default duplicate appends remain available. CHANGELOG regeneration will therefore describe the compatibility boundary rather than implying unconditional deduplication."
  "2026-08-28T09:00:53.893Z","harness:codex","Terminal receipt refresh: pm test pm-ea1yh2 --run --progress passed all 4/4 commands after every later review correction: contract snapshot plus SDK surface, exact repository coverage at 100/100/100/100, CI=1 tracker-context static quality, and the focused SDK/CLI/MCP annotation bundle at 231/231. The recorded run has zero failure categories."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T23:54:25.697Z","harness:codex","Implementation boundary: equality is resolved-author plus normalized stored text under the item writer lock. Only explicit ifAbsent requests emit top-level changed; default append response shape and intentional duplicate behavior remain compatible. Duplicate no-ops skip item/history writes and derived search-cache refresh."
  "2026-08-28T00:46:32.227Z","harness:codex","Expanded implementation boundary: the single annotation kernel covers comments, text notes, canonicalized JSON notes, and learnings. Every transport exposes optional ifAbsent, every result exposes optional changed, exact no-ops return changed_count=0, and cache refresh is skipped without altering default duplicate-append compatibility."
learnings[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T23:54:26.211Z","harness:codex","Retry idempotency belongs inside the SDK writer lock, not in CLI or MCP adapters: preflight reads race, and transport-only dedupe diverges. Make no-op observability opt-in with changed=false and changed_count=0 to preserve default response/token contracts."
  "2026-08-28T00:46:32.700Z","harness:codex","A shared SDK primitive is incomplete until surface replication proves every sibling: public types, runtime methods, CLI flags, MCP schemas, tool parameter tables, completions, generated contracts, docs, help budgets, and tests must move together. Tracker-context execution of the full static gate is a useful negative control for missing sibling surfaces."
  "2026-08-28T04:15:15.712Z","harness:codex","A public schema-version literal is part of the SDK surface: additive parameter semantics require a minor version advance, regenerated contract fixtures, and an explicit public-surface compatibility acknowledgment."
  "2026-08-28T05:36:49.274Z","harness:codex",Dual flat/nested SDK input schemas must normalize every semantically shared option at one boundary. Hoisting only the payload but not its idempotency control silently changes behavior; nested canonical options should retain precedence.
